          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
            %em iid
            is shorthand for
            = succeed "," do
              %em independent and identically distributed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+variables"} random variables
          %p
            The notion of such random variables formalizes the idea of repeated independent coin flips or dice rolls: they are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stochastic+independence"} independent events
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability"} probability
            of each event (for example, each single coin flip) follows the same distribution.
          %p
            Another name for the same process is
            = succeed "." do
              %em Bernoulli process
